{"step_index":146,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-08-23T20:09:15Z","thinking":"**Constructing Security Framework**\n\nI'm now integrating Security, JWT, WebSocket, and Redis configurations within `backend/src/main/java/com/codeduel/config/`. The initial step involves building `JwtTokenProvider.java`, which will handle JWT token generation using claims, validation, and user extraction. This will be the foundational piece to secure and authenticate the API.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"write_to_file","args":{"CodeContent":"package com.codeduel.config;\n\nimport io.jsonwebtoken.*;\nimport io.jsonwebtoken.io.Decoders;\nimport io.jsonwebtoken.security.Keys;\nimport org.slf4j.Logger;\nimport org.slf4j.LoggerFactory;\nimport org.springframework.beans.factory.annotation.Value;\nimport org.springframework.security.core.Authentication;\nimport org.springframework.stereotype.Component;\n\nimport javax.crypto.SecretKey;\nimport java.security.Key;\nimport java.util.Date;\n\n@Component\npublic class JwtTokenProvider {\n\n    private static final Logger log = LoggerFactory.getLogger(JwtTokenProvider.class);\n\n    @Value(\"${codeduel.jwt.secret:404E635266556A586E3272357538782F413F4428472B4B6250645367566B5970}\")\n    private String jwtSecret;\n\n    @Value(\"${codeduel.jwt.expiration-ms:86400000}\") // 24h\n    private long jwtExpirationMs;\n\n    private Key key() {\n        return Keys.hmacShaKeyFor(Decoders.BASE64.decode(jwtSecret));\n    }\n\n    public String generateToken(String username, Long userId, String role) {\n        Date now = new Date();\n        Date expiryDate = new Date(now.getTime() + jwtExpirationMs);\n\n        return Jwts.builder()\n                .subject(username)\n                .claim(\"userId\", userId)\n                .claim(\"role\", role)\n                .issuedAt(now)\n                .expiration(expiryDate)\n                .signWith(key())\n                .compact();\n    }\n\n    public String getUsernameFromJwt(String token) {\n        Claims claims = Jwts.parser()\n                .verifyWith((SecretKey) key())\n                .build()\n                .parseSignedClaims(token)\n                .getPayload();\n        return claims.getSubject();\n    }\n\n    public Long getUserIdFromJwt(String token) {\n        Claims claims = Jwts.parser()\n                .verifyWith((SecretKey) key())\n                .build()\n                .parseSignedClaims(token)\n                .getPayload();\n        Number userId = claims.get(\"userId\", Number.class);\n        return userId != null ? userId.longValue() : null;\n    }\n\n    public boolean validateToken(String authToken) {\n        try {\n            Jwts.parser()\n                    .verifyWith((SecretKey) key())\n                    .build()\n                    .parseSignedClaims(authToken);\n            return true;\n        } catch (MalformedJwtException ex) {\n            log.error(\"Invalid JWT token: {}\", ex.getMessage());\n        } catch (ExpiredJwtException ex) {\n            log.error(\"Expired JWT token: {}\", ex.getMessage());\n        } catch (UnsupportedJwtException ex) {\n            log.error(\"Unsupported JWT token: {}\", ex.getMessage());\n        } catch (IllegalArgumentException ex) {\n            log.error(\"JWT claims string is empty: {}\", ex.getMessage());\n        }\n        return false;\n    }\n}\n","Description":"JwtTokenProvider component","Overwrite":true,"TargetFile":"C:\\Users\\rajan\\.gemini\\antigravity\\scratch\\codeduel\\backend\\src\\main\\java\\com\\codeduel\\config\\JwtTokenProvider.java","toolAction":"Creating JwtTokenProvider.java","toolSummary":"Write JwtTokenProvider"}}]}
